\f1\fs22 The explosion, the tank, a squad of Elvi in camouflage ponchos\'97all GI Blues series by the look of them; everything moved too fast for Tony. Out of the rubble of the studio, he was escorted between two rows of more Elvi standing in some kind of judo poses, into the back of an ageing Cadillac.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The trip was fast, and would have tripped the spreadsheet alerts of any insurance risk assessor, until the drew up to a pair of ornate gates which caged an expansive manicured lawn surrounding a colonial mansion. A Cadillac door opened and Tony understood he was to get out.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>A honour guard escorted Tony up the drive to the building\'97one of those tourist trap concerns the Airborne seemed to revel in. Tony saw the building was thirsty for a lick of paint; the nearer they approached, the more the lawns appeared to be chopped up, like someone had run a race of Shetland ponies across it. At the portico Tony\'92s Elvi guard halted. In the middle of them, Tony stopped too.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>A gleaming white town car and three gleaming white suburbans came up the drive at a regally slow pace; the gravel under tyres gave little crunch. A dozen crisply-dressed professionals alighted from the suburbans; a woman who looked like an ageing Hollywood actress emerged from the town car and led the immaculately pressed business suits past Tony\'92s guard and into the mansion. Once they were inside, one of Tony\'92s guards told him, \'91Go inside. Wait in the lobby.\'92\
