\f1\fs22 When the ageing Hollywood actress bid Tony come join them in, he was clueless as to who or what was behind the door.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Tony!\'92 Sarah cried, but it seemed to Tony a weak cry. Sarah appeared somehow diminished.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The Hollywood actress said something then left; her entourage filed out.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Sarah!\'92 Tony opened his arms expecting a hug. What he got was the floor, which came up so fast, it briefly distracted him from the intensifying sting of his face. He tested it with tentative finger pressure. \'91What the tax, Sarah? I think you broke my cheek bone.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah shook her knuckles out. \'91Oh, I\'92m sorry,\'92 she said, breathing fire. \'91Never mind; I\'92m sure it\'92ll be good as fresh in a couple of hours.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony picked himself off the floor, still exploring his dented face. \'91What are you talking about?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Every day for a month, I\'92ve watched them torture you on broadcast, and every day you bounce back, as pink as if you just come from a manicure, a sauna and a blow-dry.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Yeah, I\'92ve been feeling like a colt lately, apart from the daily\'97\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah shoved Tony in the chest and sat him in the couch, which almost tipped back with the force. \'91Lately? Lately!\'92 she blared. \'91Yeah, ever since you raped me while I was asleep.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91What? What the tax? I never\'97\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Don\'92t lie to me! That night, after the Vegas Show, you took advantage of me. I was drunk and you took me \'85 while I was unconscious! Oh, Tony, I should have known a sleaze-bag cleaner\'97a Cloudborne\'97would turn out \'85\'92 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Sarah, I swear,\'92 Tony pleaded from the couch while Sarah stood over him. \'91I would never hurt you. Look, I passed out straight away that night. Slept solid till morning.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Maybe you attacked me and you don\'92t remember.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Nah, I was smashed, I woulda been out all night. I know it.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah sniffled and thought, dredging for ways she could stay angry. \'91Then why\'92d you slink off in the morning? You didn\'92t even say good-bye.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I went to get you coffee. I got picked up while I was out looking for coffee.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Well, that doesn\'92t explain \'85 you!\'92 Sarah gestured at Tony as if she meant everything about him.\
