<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah\'92s blood chilled. She felt like a King-Kong-sized mitt had grabbed her and was waving her at some angry bi-planes. She always knew crazy people would come looking for her sooner or later. She was beginning to understand feeling invincible does make it so. If the sages were the cause of her pregnancy, there remained the issue of her deeper secret. \'91That still doesn\'92t explain your \'85 regenerative properties.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Sarah, it\'92s the disc. What else could it be? Think about it: everything has been going haywire since I \'85 found it.\'92 Tony repressed visions of the blue-suited corpse on the street. \'91It makes the ground shake, it crashes vans, and it nearly buried itself in your \'85\'92 he waved in the general co-ordinates of Sarah\'92s breasts. \'91Then it glued itself to my fingers. It\'92s like it\'92s alive, one time scaly like a crocodile, then next time all slobbery like a hungry beast.\'92\
